{"kind":"report","text":"R12 rulings: rate windows (answers 8b1ec414; for request 303772df).\n\n1. Scope: confirmed. Windows apply at public ingress: parentless creation, signed reads and joins. Internal verified child sends keep the R1 and R2 authority gates and get no invented counter.\n2. Joins: keep the existing failed-check window, and add a verified-key window that also counts joins with no address (hosted agents, service bindings) by key. An invalid actor signature never charges the victim key.\n3. Accounting: creation and signed-read windows count every attempt that passes the cheap form checks, charged once before target or proof work, per verified key and per trusted edge address (null for internal calls). Native fresh authentication still runs.\n4. Defaults, as deployment settings: creation 10 per key and 30 per address per hour; signed reads 240 per key and 600 per address per minute. Measure the signed reads of a page startup and an MCP agent's startup, report the counts in the head, and raise the read defaults if a startup needs more than a third of them.\n5. Placement: confirmed. One deployment-scoped fixed serving object; a separate method on the R2 index object is acceptable. State its memory bound and what eviction or a restart resets; a reset is a named limit, and the head does not call per-isolate counting global. has() stays read-only and is never an admission cache.\n6. Wire: confirmed. A signed read over its window answers 429 with a ReadRefusal code `rate-limited`. No fabricated forbidden, no native judgment, and no change to historical native rules. A new reason code is a kernel addition: the head cites docs/kernel.md section 7 and states why the code belongs in the contract.","body":{"to":"builder"}}